<title>DENMARK: Danish April yr/yr CPI up 1.5 pct (EU method).</title>
<headline>Danish April yr/yr CPI up 1.5 pct (EU method).</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish consumer prices were 0.3 percent higher in April 1997 from March 1997 and 1.5 percent up on April 1996, the National Statistics Office said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The CPI data was issued under new EU-harmonised calculation methods. Under the traditional Danish national formula the respective figures would have been a 0.3 percent month-on-month rise and 1.7 percent up year-on-year.  </p>
<p>    NEW EU FORMULA	     April 1997   March 1997  April 1996</p>
<p>    Change on month (pct)     +0.3	    +0.1	  +0.3</p>
<p>    Change on year (pct)	+1.5	    +1.5	  +1.7</p>
<p>    Index (base 1994)	   101.4	   101.1	 99.9</p>
<p>NATIONAL FORMULA</p>
<p>    Change on month (pct)     +0.3		0.0	 +0.3</p>
<p>    Change on year (pct)	+1.7	     +1.7	 +2.0</p>
<p>    Index (base 1980)	   202.7	    202.1	199.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' average expectations were for a 1.8 percent yr/yr rise from April 1996 according to the national formula.</p>
<p>-- Chris Follett, Copenhagen Newsroom +45-33-969652</p>
</text>
